  "slug": "carcinoma-cell-carcinoma-9b72",
  "summary": "Public bulk and single-cell cohorts are now routinely combined to prioritise candidate markers, with functional follow-up beginning to appear.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is integration of bulk transcriptomic and single-cell data, increasingly with proteomic, spatial or epigenomic layers, to nominate prognostic, diagnostic or immune-associated biomarkers. Most items draw on public resources such as TCGA, GEO and CPTAC, applying differential expression, machine-learning risk scores and immune infiltration profiling, and the evidence remains largely retrospective and exploratory. The MOFA+ preprint is distinctive in jointly factorising paired scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq from two NMIBC patients, identifying a BCG-associated HSPC factor with candidate signatures. What is newer is experimental follow-up in a subset of items: GSTP1 and MAN1B1 are supported by functional validation, NR1D2 and FAM72D by siRNA knockdown, and GULP1 is linked to lipid-driven reprogramming of CD36+ PD-L1+ tumour-associated macrophages in anti-PD-1 resistance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-12"
}
